## Governance

Git hooks, lint config, and CI workflows are governed by
[project-starter-template](https://github.com/carpet-stain/project-starter-template)
(PST) under the delivery ladder
([ADR-0006](https://github.com/carpet-stain/project-starter-template/blob/main/docs/adr/0006-the-delivery-ladder-drift-rule-and-channel-invariants.md)):
live reusable workflows and `remotes:`-fetched hooks stay current on their
own; everything else PST-owned is listed in `.pst-sync.yml` and lands as a
PR when PST cuts a release. Those configs (`lefthook.yml`, `justfile`,
`.pst-sync.yml` itself) are the enforced spec — this file points at them
rather than restating their contents. To keep a local deviation instead of
reconciling the next sync PR, flip that file's entry to `owned: true` in
`.pst-sync.yml`.

Workflow, commit rules, and tooling this repo inherited at scaffold time:
[PST's git-flow README](https://github.com/carpet-stain/project-starter-template/blob/main/git-flow/README.md).

